@format 1
@id split.sidecar-restore
@title Restore sections from sidecar
@area UI workflow
@entry input
@summary Read stored sections for newly opened media and apply valid records without writing them back during restoration.
@section I. UI
@tabs Split
@flow TB
@related preview.open-media, shared.synchronize-sections
@tag section
@tag sidecar
@tag restore

@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow
@alias sidecar = Cadroue.Media.LSidecarStore

[input] Timeline attaches media <input>
- Request section restoration for the active source @ flow.PFlowSidecarRestore(...)
> read

[read] Read sidecar <decision>
- Resolve and read the source sidecar @ sidecar.LSidecarRead(...)
? "A sidecar contains sections" > apply
? "No sidecar sections are available" > empty
? "The sidecar cannot be read" > failed

[apply] Apply stored sections <process>
- Mark restoration so synchronization cannot rewrite the same sidecar @ flow.PFlowSidecarApply(...)
- Convert stored section records into timeline segments @ flow.PFlowSidecarApply(...)
- Keep only sections valid for the active media duration @ flow.PFlowSectionsSet(...)
> fragment:shared.synchronize-sections

[empty] Nothing to restore <output>
= The newly attached timeline starts with no sections.

[failed] Restore failed <error>
- Record the sidecar restoration failure @ flow.PFlowSidecarRestore(...)
= The media remains open with an empty section list.
